<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Pigneau de Behaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1741">1741</a>–<a href="/years/1799">1799</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Bishop of Adran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Pigneau de Behaine was a French Catholic missionary and titular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Adran who supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Nguyen Anh</a> in his war against the Tay Son. In 1787 he negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> promising French military aid, and when the French government failed to honour it he raised volunteers and supplies himself. He died in 1799 during the siege of Qui Nhon, three years before Nguyen Anh became Emperor Gia Long.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-pigneau-de-behaine.jpg" alt="Pierre Pigneau de Behaine" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eugénie Marie Salanson / After Maupérin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_de_Mgr_Pigneaux_de_Behaine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
